WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.340
Do you have something you need to be doing
right now but are avoiding like the Plague?

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.140
Maybe you have a lot of stuff you need to
do but you just keep putting it off, and,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.010
you distract yourself from the discomfort
of even thinking about it?

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.039
Have you ever thought about what it would
feel like if you actually completed all of

00:00:13.039 --> 00:00:14.039
it?

00:00:14.039 --> 00:00:17.619
Like you just took a day, from the moment
you woke up till the end of the day, you worked

00:00:17.619 --> 00:00:21.390
hard, through motivation and determination,
and just crushed everything on your to-do

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.390
list?

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:23.390
Today we're going to talk about that.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:32.200
I'm Joey and welcome to Better Ideas.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.320
Being massively productive over a long period
of time can seem like an activity that many

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.320
people lack the motivation or focus to pull
off.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.210
But what a lot of people don't realize is
they don't actually lack motivation or focus,

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:47.829
they're just not setting the right parameters
to foster an environment of productivity and

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:48.829
focus.

00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:52.420
In order to have a day where you're massively
productive from start to finish - you have

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.289
to set yourself up for success.

00:00:54.289 --> 00:00:58.171
So here are 5 techniques that I use when I
really need to get stuff done, and when I

00:00:58.171 --> 00:01:02.440
use them together I notice I'm just far more
focused, far more motivated, and I actually

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.890
end up crushing everything on my to-do list.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:09.500
Also, disclaimer: These techniques work best
for homework, office work, paperwork, anything

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.470
where you can sit down at a coffee shop or
at a desk.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.659
Number One: Find your Sacred Space.

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:19.720
The Sacred Space is your particular geographical
location that you treat with the utmost respect.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.110
It's your temple of productivity.

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:25.229
It could be a particular coffee shop that
you notice you work really well in, or it

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:28.930
could even be a certain corner in your house
that you notice you just have extra focus

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:29.930
in.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:33.430
You just have to make sure that when you're
there, it's for studying and studying only.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:38.100
Once you goof off in that spot - you've officially
desecrated the sacred place and it's no longer

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.250
sacred - you have to find a different place.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.240
You ruined it.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.280
My second technique is - Start Your Work First
Thing in the Morning.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.620
If you're really serious about getting work
done that day, and it's really important to

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.990
you, don't check social media first thing
in the morning, don't go on your phone - just

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:56.130
go to the sacred space as soon as possible
and start hitting the books and getting to

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.130
work.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.229
As I've mentioned in previous videos, willpower
is a finite resource that depletes with every

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.590
single decision you make throughout the day,
so, in the morning, you have an abundant amount

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.540
of willpower that you can use at your disposal.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:13.480
So just channel that glorious amount of willpower,
and just hyper-focus it into being productive.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.510
Step number three is to Make A Proper Checklist.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:19.800
You need a roadmap as to where you're going
- and making a good checklist is a lot more

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.710
than just writing all your tasks in random
order and putting a little tick-box next to

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:25.710
them.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:28.910
You have to organize, prioritize and streamline
every single thing on that list into it's

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:29.910
most basic component.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:34.270
I get into a lot more detail on how, exactly,
to make this checklist in a previous video

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:35.710
(I'll put the link in the description).

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.360
Number four is to use the Pomodoro Technique.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.760
(Pomodoro technique...

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.100
I don't really know how to pronounce it.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.100
Pomodro?...

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.100
Pomo-door-oh?...

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.100
Pum-oh-diroh...

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.100
Totoro.)

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:49.300
So basically you work for 25 minutes and take
a 5 minute break doing some type of non-mentally-hyperactive

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.300
activity.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:54.349
This reduces the amount of mental strain associated
with high levels of concentration and allows

00:02:54.349 --> 00:02:56.030
you to work harder for longer.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:59.920
Technique number Five is to Set a Final Alarm
to the particular time that you need to start

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.260
thinking about something else.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.580
Now this one seems kind of obvious, but a
lot of people neglect it and don't really

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.580
realize its importance.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.650
I know in my own life - when I have a meeting
or a class sometime late at night and I'm

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.790
trying to get homework done earlier in that
day, I'm always thinking of that looming thing

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.710
I have to do, and not all my attention is
focused on my present work.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:21.520
So in order to have the most effective work
session, you have to really free up things

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:25.720
like that - free up mental RAM, don't think
about the things you have to do in the future,

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:26.930
just focus on the now.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:31.000
So that's why you have to delegate the mental
RAM or your responsibilities - to things like

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.000
alarms.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.000
So once you set that in place, you don't have
to worry about it anymore - you can focus

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:41.530
100% of your attention on the task at hand
and really get things done and hone your focus.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.930
Most people are familiar with at least one
of these techniques - but very few people

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.500
use all of them at the same time.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:50.710
And the people I do know who've incorporated
3 or more of these things into their dail

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.480
work routine are some of the most productive
people I've ever met.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:58.040
So give it a try - maybe you have a dark cloud
of looming responsiblities hanging over you

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.310
causing you to be stressed, anxious, whatever...

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:04.710
Well, by properly utilizing these techniques
and incorportating them in your study or work

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:08.410
session - you can be sure that your focus
will be honed, your productivity game will

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:12.560
be off the charts, so you can chip away at
that mountain of responsibilities until it's

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.710
a little pile of dust lying at the feet of
you - the victor.

